#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:96
msgid ""
"Pick a profile and you are done. «Maximum detection» is recommended for small microplastics in "
"high-resolution microscopy photos."
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:109
msgid "Min. confidence (conf):"
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:118
msgid "0.05–0.95. Higher = fewer detections (and fewer false positives)."
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:122
msgid "IoU NMS:"
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:130
msgid "0.30–0.70. Suppresses overlapping boxes."
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:133 src/polyx/gui/trainer/pages/parameters.py:73
msgid "Image size (imgsz):"
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:151
msgid ""
"Larger = detects smaller particles (key for microplastics), but slower and heavier on GPU "
"memory. For high-resolution photos go up to 4096+. The button probes the maximum your GPU can "
"take with the loaded model."
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:169
msgid "'mps' = the Mac's built-in GPU (Apple Silicon). 'cpu' = processor."
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:171
msgid "This is an Intel Mac: 'cpu' only. MPS requires Apple Silicon."
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:184
msgid ""
"A full-plate photo enters the network rescaled to imgsz: at 4096 px reduced to 2080, every "
"particle shrinks by half and disappears below the network stride. With tiling, each tile enters "
"at native resolution and the boxes return to full-photo coordinates, merged with a global NMS — "
"nothing has to be cut by hand nor the counts added up afterwards."
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:193
msgid "When to tile:"
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:199
msgid "automatic"
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:200
msgid "always"
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:201
msgid "never"
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:208
msgid "«auto» decides on its own from the longest side of each photo."
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:211
msgid "Threshold (longest side, px):"
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:220
msgid ""
"Above this, tiling kicks in. 2000 lets the study crops (1630 px) through whole and tiles the "
"full plates (~4096 px)."
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:228
msgid "Tile side (px):"
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:237
msgid ""
"0 = automatic, min(threshold, imgsz). It should match the size of the crops the model was "
"trained on: if the model saw particles at one scale and the tile presents them at another, "
"recall drops."
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:245
msgid "Overlap between tiles:"
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:255
msgid ""
"0.25 = each tile overlaps a quarter of its neighbour. The overlap is what avoids losing or "
"duplicating a particle that falls right on the seam."
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:276
msgid "IoU for matching True Positives:"
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:284
msgid "COCO standard: 0.50. Stricter: 0.75."
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:288
msgid ""
"True Positives: correct class + IoU ≥ threshold.  False Positives: prediction with no nearby GT."
"  False Negatives: GT not detected.  Misclassified: high IoU but wrong class."
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:300
msgid "µm per pixel:"
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:312
msgid "Fallback: used only when the dish cannot be measured. 0 = no calibration."
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:330
msgid "Actual dish diameter (mm):"
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:338
msgid "Nominal outer diameter. The Petri dish used in this study is 100 mm."
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:341
msgid "Dish height (mm):"
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:349
msgid "0 = no correction. A 100 mm Petri dish is usually 15 mm tall."
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:352
msgid "Camera-to-base distance (mm):"
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:360
msgid "0 = no correction. Measure to the BOTTOM of the dish, not to its rim."
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:366
msgid ""
"Nothing has to be marked: the dish rim is found automatically. The radius comes from fitting a "
"circle to the rim sampled along 720 directions, with outlier rejection; the Hough transform only"
" supplies the approximate centre, because its radius can be off by as much as 12 %. In crops the"
" dish is not visible, so there the scale is inherited from the calibration index left behind "
"when the crop was made."
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:373
msgid ""
"The dish rim sits closer to the camera than the base where the particles lie, so it projects "
"larger and the resulting scale is too small: left uncorrected, ALL sizes are underestimated. "
"With a 15 mm dish and the camera at 100 mm that is almost 16 percentage points; at 500 mm, about"
" 3 %. Fill in both fields above to correct it."
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:380
msgid ""
"The detector computes the area and equivalent diameter (of a circle with the same area) for "
"every detected particle. With calibration, also in μm and μm²."
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:392
msgid "Min size (µm):"
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:400
msgid "Max size (µm):"
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:407
msgid "0 = no filter. Applies to the equivalent diameter."
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:416
msgid "Minimum confidence to assign:"
msgstr ""

#: src/polyx/gui/detector/pages/parameters.py:426
msgid ""
"0 = off. Below this value the particle is still counted, but reported as \"unassignable\" "
"instead of being given a polymer. Nile Red responds to the polarity of its environment, not to "
"chemical identity: it separates PET —a polyester— cleanly from the rest, while PP and LDPE are "
"both polyolefins and differ only in brightness, which depends on exposure and focus. Abstaining "
"is more honest than inventing the class, and the report states what percentage was left "
"unassigned."
msgstr ""

